WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.159 --> 00:00:07.029
Pawn Stars fans were caught by surprise in
early 2016 when series star Austin Lee Russell,

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:10.700
better known as "Chumlee," was arrested for
drug and weapon possession as part of an ongoing

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.000
sexual assault investigation.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.869
The truth is, we never really know the people
we like seeing on TV.

00:00:16.869 --> 00:00:20.240
Time to put the hawking on hold as we look
at the untold truth about the cast of Pawn

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:21.500
Stars.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:23.840
HUMAN SKULLS AND JAPANESE PORN

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:27.840
According to Rick Harrison, co-owner of the
World Famous Gold &amp; Silver Pawn Shop, his

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:31.390
business has seen all kinds of weird items
come and go.

00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:35.440
Surprisingly, human skulls and bizarre types
of Japanese pornography are the oddest items

00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.531
anyone has ever brought into his shop to sell—which,
if you think about it, means he's kind of

00:00:39.531 --> 00:00:41.550
gotten off easy over the years.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:43.090
UNREAL REALITY

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.680
What you see on TV isn't quite what you get.

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.670
Given that attempting to film the actual day-to-day
life at a pawn shop would result in some pretty

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:53.640
boring television, it should come as no surprise
that the items you see brought into the Gold

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:56.859
&amp; Silver Pawn Shop on the show have been vetted
beforehand.

00:00:56.859 --> 00:01:00.059
This allows the guys to bring in all kinds
of experts who help them decide a fair price

00:01:00.059 --> 00:01:01.059
for the items.

00:01:01.059 --> 00:01:05.289
Additionally, due partly to Nevada privacy
laws, the Pawn Stars crew is prevented from

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:08.350
working at the actual Gold &amp; Silver counter
while the cameras roll.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:12.380
Instead, they film their scenes on a set that's
been designed to look like the store.

00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:15.580
It's no surprise that not all the gold and
silver you see on your screen is the real

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:16.700
deal.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.560
RICK MARRIED INTO A MESS

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.420
After Harrison wed legal worker Deanna Burditt
in 2013, tabloids reported that the lovebirds

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:27.360
were embroiled in a legal battle involving
Burditt's ex-husband, who was free on bail

00:01:27.360 --> 00:01:31.060
while awaiting trial for a variety of sex-related
charges.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.929
Deanna's ex was ultimately sentenced up to
15 years in prison for his offenses.

00:01:34.929 --> 00:01:37.140
FIRED FOR BEING NAKED (SORTA)

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.970
Pawn Stars cast member Olivia Black lost her
gig on the show after nude photos of her surfaced,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:45.080
exposing her previous career as a model for
SuicideGirls.

00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:48.770
She later revealed that she was still an employee
of the store, as she was really only "fired"

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:50.459
in front of the cameras.

00:01:50.459 --> 00:01:53.780
Black resumed her modeling career and sued
to get back on the show, ultimately leaving

00:01:53.780 --> 00:01:56.600
her job at the store several months later.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.970
SUED FOR MELTING STOLEN COINS

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.640
When you deal with the public for a living,
you really never know what's going to happen.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:06.610
Harrison got a harsh reminder of this in 2014,
when his store was sued for melting down a

00:02:06.610 --> 00:02:10.200
collection of gold coins that their former
owner alleged had been stolen and sold off

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.720
by his niece.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:15.860
Although pawn shops in Nevada are required
to hold onto items for 30 to 90 days in case

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:20.300
the owners want them back, gold coins aren't
subject to that law—meaning the lawsuit

00:02:20.300 --> 00:02:24.380
might have been an embarrassing hassle, but
it didn't pose much of a legal threat to the

00:02:24.380 --> 00:02:25.380
store.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:26.810
COREY HARRISON: STUNT CYCLIST

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:31.230
In 2014, Harrison was riding his bike while
collecting supplies for his birthday party

00:02:31.230 --> 00:02:34.980
when a piece of his fender came off, sending
him into a high-speed tailspin.

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.890
Thinking fast, he avoided sailing into traffic
by jumping off his bike—and he still went

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:42.440
to the party before heading to the hospital,
where he learned he had a broken hand.

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:45.850
Harrison's no stranger to wrecks, either;
in 2011, he was in the news for wiping out

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.300
in the rain during a ride between Vegas and
San Diego.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:51.470
Maybe it's time to start pawning the bikes.

00:02:51.470 --> 00:02:53.740
PAWN STARS' BIG EXPANSION

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:57.870
Reality TV can be fickle, so credit is due
to Harrison for striking while the iron is

00:02:57.870 --> 00:03:02.050
hot and using his fame as the foundation for
a business empire that now includes "Pawn

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:05.481
Plaza," a shopping center made out of old
shipping containers that sits next door to

00:03:05.481 --> 00:03:06.481
the shop.

00:03:06.481 --> 00:03:10.570
Among the tenants: Rick's Rollin' Smoke Barbecue
&amp; Tavern, where Harrison intends to sit in

00:03:10.570 --> 00:03:12.730
as a part-time bartender.

00:03:12.730 --> 00:03:14.290
INTERNET DEATH HOAX

00:03:14.290 --> 00:03:18.630
In the spring of 2013, word circulated that
Chumlee died of a heart attack.

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:21.950
These rumors were quickly debunked with a
tweet from the Pawn Stars cast member, who

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:25.180
told followers, "May we live long, Rich forever."

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.880
Time to start spending those riches on a good
lawyer.

00:03:27.880 --> 00:03:29.320
NOT CHUMLEE'S FIRST RODEO

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:33.940
In 2012, cameras captured Chumlee in a brawl
with an unidentified man who approached him

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:37.069
and a group of friends while they were hanging
out on Hollywood Boulevard.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:40.569
He later insisted he was fighting in self-defense,
and that the man was a stranger who was trying

00:03:40.569 --> 00:03:42.310
to climb into his car.

00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:45.100
"Self-defense" isn't a bad way to talk your
way out of a scuffle.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:48.630
But good luck explaining the meth, the gun,
and everything else, Chumlee.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.790
Thanks for watching!

